# File Standards

## File Naming Conventions

| Type | Pattern | Examples |
|------|---------|----------|
| Managers | `[Function]Manager.cs` | `WaveManager.cs`, `GridManager.cs` |
| Components | `[Entity][Function].cs` | `TileVisuals.cs`, `CubeAudio.cs` |
| Data | `[Type]Data.cs` | `WaveData.cs`, `StageData.cs` |
| Systems | `[Function]System.cs` | `PlayerMarkerSystem.cs` |
| Utilities | `[Function]Utils.cs` | `GridUtils.cs`, `MathUtils.cs` |
| Interfaces | `I[Capability].cs` | `IManagerDebugInterface.cs` |

## Required Region Structure

All MonoBehaviour classes must follow this organization:

```csharp
using Sirenix.OdinInspector;
using DG.Tweening;
using static Enumerations;

public class ExampleManager : MonoBehaviour
{
    #region Inspector Configuration
    // Use Odin attributes for organization
    [Title("Configuration")]
    [SerializeField] private float speed = 5f;
    
    [FoldoutGroup("Advanced")]
    [SerializeField] private bool useAdvanced = false;
    #endregion

    #region Manager References
    // Cached manager references (assigned in Start)
    private WaveManager waveManager;
    #endregion

    #region Runtime State
    // Private fields for runtime state
    private bool isInitialized;
    private Tween activeTween;  // DOTween reference
    #endregion

    #region Properties
    // Public properties, singleton Instance
    public static ExampleManager Instance { get; private set; }
    #endregion

    #region Unity Lifecycle
    // Awake, Start, Update, OnDestroy
    // CRITICAL: Kill DOTweens in OnDestroy
    private void OnDestroy()
    {
        activeTween?.Kill();
        DOTween.Kill(transform);
    }
    #endregion

    #region Public API
    // Public methods with [Button] for testing
    [Button("Do Action")]
    public void DoAction() { /* ... */ }
    #endregion

    #region Private Methods
    // Internal implementation methods
    #endregion

    #region Debug
    [FoldoutGroup("Debug")]
    [SerializeField] private bool enableDebugLogs = true;
    
    [FoldoutGroup("Debug"), Button("Log Status")]
    private void LogStatus() => this.Log("Status", enableDebugLogs);
    #endregion
}
```

### Odin Organization Guidelines

| Section | Odin Attribute | Notes |
|---------|---------------|-------|
| Main config | `[Title("Name")]` | Top-level section headers |
| Related fields | `[BoxGroup("Name")]` | Visual grouping |
| Optional/Advanced | `[FoldoutGroup("Name")]` | Collapsed by default |
| Complex inspectors | `[TabGroup]` | Multiple tabs |
| Debug section | `[FoldoutGroup("Debug")]` | Always collapsible |

### When to Use Odin vs Regions

- **Use regions**: Code organization (always required)
- **Use Odin attributes**: Inspector organization (in addition to regions)
- **Both work together**: Regions organize code, Odin organizes inspector

## File Size Limits

| Type | Max Lines | Action When Approaching |
|------|-----------|------------------------|
| Core Components | 750 | Plan decomposition at 500 |
| Manager Classes | 600 | Plan decomposition at 400 |
| Utility Classes | 300 | Extract helpers at 200 |
| Data Classes | 300 | Split into related groups |
| Interfaces | 200 | Split by responsibility |

### Decomposition Pattern

When files exceed limits, use the Tile component pattern:
```
Before: LargeManager.cs (1000+ lines)

After:
LargeManager.cs (facade, ~200 lines)
├── LargeManagerSubsystemA.cs (specific responsibility)
├── LargeManagerSubsystemB.cs (specific responsibility)
└── LargeManagerHelpers.cs (utility methods)
```

## Complete Unit Rule

Modifications must be complete functional units:

**DO:**
- Complete methods from signature to closing brace
- Method clusters that work together
- Complete properties with getters/setters
- Entire region blocks when refactoring

**DON'T:**
- Partial method bodies
- Incomplete control structures (if/for/while)
- Individual lines within complex methods
- Half-implemented features

## Directory Structure

```
Assets/scripts/
├── Components/      # Gameplay components (Tile, Cube, etc.)
├── Data/            # ScriptableObject definitions
├── Debuggers/       # Debug tools and visualizations
├── Hub/             # Hub-specific UI and systems
├── Managers/        # Singleton managers
├── Testing/         # Test infrastructure
├── UI/              # UI components and systems
│   └── Utils/       # UI utilities (LogExtensions, etc.)
└── Utils/           # General utilities, Enumerations

Assets/data/
├── stages/          # StageData assets
├── waves/           # WaveData assets (organized by stage)
└── [other data]/    # Other ScriptableObject instances
```
